Phase 2 item 1 — proper conversation roles in the one-agent loop
=================================================================
Node: M2.7 (Basic Prompt Compiler and one-agent runtime)
Defect: Future-tasks.md section 2 item 1 (audit 2026-09-06)
Revision: commit 0f2e5e4 (branch phase2/message-roles)
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC timestamps

WHAT CHANGED
------------
one_agent.rs kept `conversation: Vec<String>` and sent every entry as a
ChatMessage::user — including the model's own prior text and tool results
flattened to "tool <name> → {json}" strings. The gateway's typed role
contract existed (M2.6) but was never used by the loop.

Now: conversation is Vec<ChatMessage>. The compiled prompt is the user
turn; each model turn is recorded as an assistant message carrying its
text and the tool calls EXACTLY as issued; every issued call is answered
by a tool-result message keyed by call id (result JSON on success; the
refusal text marked is_error for policy-denied, tool-errored and
invalid-payload calls). Invalid payloads are still rejected BEFORE side
effects. Both provider body builders serialize the typed roles
(OpenAI: assistant.tool_calls + role:"tool" keyed by tool_call_id;
Anthropic: tool_use blocks + user tool_result blocks keyed by tool_use_id).

